# Written by provision.py and by anything else that provisions against the
# local instance: the project and OIDC client, the client secret ZITADEL
# issues once at creation, test principals and their passwords. Real
# credentials, even for a throwaway container, and exactly the kind of file
# that gets committed by a hurried `git add -A`.
#
# Every `.env` here, not one named file. This listed `provisioned.env` alone
# until 2026-09-15, and `test-principals.env` -- a password in plain text --
# sat untracked and unignored in koras-e2e-shop, one `git add -A` from being
# published. A pattern that has to be extended per file is a pattern that
# will be forgotten.
*.env
